00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:39.438
- I sang with Dinosaur
Junior last December

00:18:39.438 --> 00:18:40.755
because they asked me.

00:18:40.755 --> 00:18:42.389
I did a song, "Don't,"

00:18:42.389 --> 00:18:44.408
which only has, "Why?
Why don't you like me?"

00:18:44.408 --> 00:18:46.200
so even I could get the lyric.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.224
But I did it because Jay asked me,

00:18:48.224 --> 00:18:50.255
and I don't want to disappoint those guys,

00:18:50.255 --> 00:18:52.530
and I remember afterwards, they all came

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.835
up to me like, "That was really intense."

00:18:54.835 --> 00:18:57.594
I'm like, "There's, what
other way do you do it?"

00:18:57.594 --> 00:18:59.585
- Especially with those
guys with Dinosaur Junior.

00:18:59.585 --> 00:19:01.662
- Oh it was, with Jay,
being onstage with Jay was,

00:19:01.662 --> 00:19:05.168
which is all of them, but
that much guitar volume,

00:19:05.168 --> 00:19:07.077
that was something else.

00:19:07.077 --> 00:19:09.153
'Cause I'm a fan, big fan of that band,

00:19:09.153 --> 00:19:11.571
but yeah all of that is still there,

00:19:11.571 --> 00:19:15.536
but if you're not, if what
you're pushing forward

00:19:15.536 --> 00:19:20.320
isn't all the way real, then
if it's 98% real, then the 2%

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.761
that you're lying to
the crowd, shame on you.

00:19:23.761 --> 00:19:24.964
I can't do that.

00:19:24.964 --> 00:19:28.763
This is hallowed ground for
me, and so if it's not 100%,

00:19:28.763 --> 00:19:31.303
I sadly have to walk away.

00:19:31.303 --> 00:19:34.102
- The reason I do what I do,

00:19:34.102 --> 00:19:37.117
the reasons why I get to do what I do

00:19:37.117 --> 00:19:39.450
all come from 1970 something

00:19:40.695 --> 00:19:42.279
into 1981,

00:19:42.279 --> 00:19:46.362
high school to me leaving,
punk rock, literature,

00:19:47.352 --> 00:19:51.091
poetry, realizing the
power of putting the pen

00:19:51.091 --> 00:19:53.326
to the paper and expressing yourself.

00:19:53.326 --> 00:19:56.409
That if you can write, you can write.

00:19:57.524 --> 00:19:59.739
Let's break that sentence
down for a minute.

00:19:59.739 --> 00:20:03.112
If you can form a sentence,
you can form a sentence,

00:20:03.112 --> 00:20:05.773
and it doesn't matter who you are.

00:20:05.773 --> 00:20:08.443
It doesn't matter if you're
the high school quarterback,

00:20:08.443 --> 00:20:10.536
going to be with the
pretty girl at the prom,

00:20:10.536 --> 00:20:14.494
or if you're the loser, which you're not,

00:20:14.494 --> 00:20:15.972
and the person who doesn't get picked

00:20:15.972 --> 00:20:18.943
to be on the basketball team at gym,

00:20:18.943 --> 00:20:23.481
you can write, and you
can have as much authority

00:20:23.481 --> 00:20:27.064
over your own writing
as Flannery O'Connor,

00:20:28.159 --> 00:20:31.503
Earnest Hemingway, or
anyone you can imagine.

00:20:31.503 --> 00:20:35.201
You can have your own, and
you will find in your life

00:20:35.201 --> 00:20:37.469
that some of the only real true freedom

00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:39.601
you'll ever get is your imagination,

00:20:39.601 --> 00:20:42.587
your thoughts, and what
you can put on the paper,

00:20:42.587 --> 00:20:44.847
and the good news is you never, ever,

00:20:44.847 --> 00:20:47.025
ever have to show it to anyone.

00:20:47.025 --> 00:20:49.866
It can be like a meditation
that you can write to yourself.

00:20:49.866 --> 00:20:51.803
You can be as angry as you want.

00:20:51.803 --> 00:20:53.378
You can make up anything you want.

00:20:53.378 --> 00:20:57.760
You are never freer than
when you're putting it down

00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:00.547
and I always say pen and
paper because I have an analog

00:21:00.547 --> 00:21:03.835
relationship with writing,
but if you want to key it in,

00:21:03.835 --> 00:21:07.918
you can do that too, and
you can be a 53 year old

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:13.109
man like me and still do a
journal entry every day as I do

00:21:13.109 --> 00:21:16.961
because it is part of my way
is to check in with myself.

00:21:16.961 --> 00:21:18.181
Hey Henry, how you doing?

00:21:18.181 --> 00:21:21.341
Well, I'm pretty sad
today because of this,

00:21:21.341 --> 00:21:23.500
and I'm very angry about this.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.124
There's a lot of writing I do

00:21:25.124 --> 00:21:27.558
volumes of it that no one sees.

00:21:27.558 --> 00:21:28.509
I never publish it.

00:21:28.509 --> 00:21:30.829
I just need to check in with myself

00:21:30.829 --> 00:21:34.079
through the hand, the ink to the paper,

00:21:35.077 --> 00:21:38.424
and anyone can do that and
you never have to show it

00:21:38.424 --> 00:21:41.806
to anyone, not your significant other,

00:21:41.806 --> 00:21:45.137
not your brothers or sisters
or parents or teachers.

00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:47.470
It can be exclusively yours.

